 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+### Decisions — `adrs/`
+
+Explanation of lasting choices that constrain the system's structure or operation. Record a choice when future
+maintainers need the incident, competing options and tradeoffs to judge whether its reasons still hold; routine
+implementation choices belong in code and review. Each record has Context, Options, Decision and Consequences,
+in that order, and a numbered filename `NNNN-<decision>.md`. The [decisions guide](adrs/README.md) lists them.
+
+### Architecture — `architecture.md`
+
+Explanation of the system's current parts, boundaries and connections. It owns the topology and links to decision
+records for the reasons behind structural choices. It has Parts and How they connect, in that order.
+See [Architecture](architecture.md).
+
+### Features — `features/`
+
+Reference for current member-facing behavior and its rules. Each page describes one feature in subject-specific
+sections and links the decisions that shaped it. The [features guide](features/README.md) lists them.
+
+### Runbooks — `runbooks/`
+
+How-to guidance for an operational trigger. Each page identifies its operator and owner, then has Before you begin,
+Steps with expected results, and If it fails. The [runbooks guide](runbooks/README.md) lists them.
+
+## Glossary
+
+[Glossary](glossary.md) owns shared names. Each entry gives the preferred term, its meaning and rejected synonyms
+under `_Avoid_`.
+
+Each fact has one owner: other pages link to it. Every page opens with who reads it, when and why it exists.
